Microsoft's Pragmatic Rust Guidelines and the Rust API Guidelines informed the design and remain linked reference authorities rather than vendored manuals:
https://github.com/microsoft/rust-guidelines/tree/9585e288d21d2da994a0550c926a09b62d79f8bd
https://rust-lang.github.io/api-guidelines/

The adaptation retains selective reference loading and ownership, error, and tooling guidance. It replaces fixed Copy-size thresholds, blanket panic restrictions, one-assertion preferences, and restricted dynamic-dispatch rules with decisions based on the actual contract. Existing testing and performance policies govern when extra checks are warranted. Tool choices remain conditional, and repository/MSRV constraints take precedence over upstream defaults. Async runtime guidance remains in the installed runtime's documentation until a focused reference is justified.

